    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0721" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p2/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">792.5 MSP/12–1153:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 409<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Thailand (Parsons) to the Department of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-12-11T17:00:00+07:00">December 11, 1953—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1186. Reference Embtel 1139, December 7.</p>
                <p>Part IV of IV—MAAG.</p>
                <p>This message summarizes MAAG recommendations
                    carried Ambassador Donovan.</p>
                <p>Concur recommendations General Gillmore to JCS.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d409-f1"/> Particularly anxious (1) for
                    despatch psychological warfare officers due their relationship other
                    political-psychological program approved Thai (see reference telegram) and (2)
                    attempt through MAAG install competent United
                    States budget officers Thai military departments.</p>
                <pb facs="0722" n="702" xml:id="pg702"/>
                <p>Recommend furnish “soft” goods—clothing, shoes with approximate total cost $2.5
                    million.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Parsons</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="1" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is to the Report of the U.S. Joint Military Mission to Thailand,
                    attached to <ref target="#d404">Document 404</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
